# Code Examples - Proper Formatting Standards

This rule provides concrete examples of properly formatted code that follows our ESLint standards.

## Vue Component Structure

```vue
<template>
  <div class="example-component">
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    <p v-if="showDescription">{{ description }}</p>
    <button 
      class="action-button"
      @click="handleClick"
    >
      Click Me
    </button>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'ExampleComponent',
  
  props: {
    title: {
      type: String,
      required: true
    },
    description: {
      type: String,
      default: ''
    }
  },
  
  data () {
    return {
      showDescription: false
    }
  },
  
  computed: {
    computedValue () {
      return this.title.toUpperCase()
    }
  },
  
  methods: {
    handleClick () {
      this.showDescription = !this.showDescription
      this.$emit('button-clicked')
    }
  }
}
</script>

<style>
.example-component {
  padding: 16px;
  background-color: #f5f5f5;
}

.action-button {
  margin-top: 8px;
  padding: 8px 16px;
}
</style>
```

## JavaScript Function Examples

```js
// Good: Space before function parentheses
function doSomething () {
  return true
}

// Good: Proper arrow function formatting
const arrowFunction = (param1, param2) => {
  const result = param1 + param2
  return result
}

// Good: Object formatting
const user = {
  name: 'John',
  age: 30,
  address: {
    street: '123 Main St',
    city: 'Anytown'
  }
}

// Good: Array formatting
const items = [
  'item1',
  'item2',
  'item3'
]

// Good: Conditional statements
if (condition) {
  doSomething()
} else if (otherCondition) {
  doSomethingElse()
} else {
  doDefault()
}

// Good: Proper spacing in function calls
calculateTotal(price, tax, discount)

// Good: Method chaining
const result = array
  .filter(item => item.active)
  .map(item => item.name)
  .join(', ')
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

```js
// BAD: Missing space before function parentheses
function badFunction() {
  return true;
}

// BAD: Semicolons and trailing spaces  
const value = 'example';   

// BAD: Inconsistent quotes
const mixed = "single and double quotes don't mix well";

// BAD: Improper spacing around operators
const sum=value1+value2;

// BAD: No spaces inside braces
const badObject={foo:bar};

// GOOD VERSIONS:
function goodFunction () {
  return true
}

const value = 'example'

const consistent = 'single quotes are preferred'

const sum = value1 + value2

const goodObject = { foo: bar }
```
